## Scenarios

### bootstrap reason planner v2

#### admits only the Stage 3 and Stage 4 targets

- Verify: admits only the Stage 3 and Stage 4 targets
   - Expected: rc3 equals `0`
   - Expected: rt_file_exists(receipt) is true
   - Expected: rc4 equals `0`
   - Expected: rcR equals `2`
   - Expected: rcA equals `2`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 22 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-GEN-COMPILER-001
step("Verify: admits only the Stage 3 and Stage 4 targets")
val receipt = "build/land11_spec_fx/planner_stage3_receipt.txt"
if rt_file_exists(receipt):
    rt_file_delete(receipt)
val (out3, rc3) = run_planner("//bootstrap:stage3", "seed-missing", receipt,
    sha64("a"), sha64("b"), sha64("c"), sha64("d"))
expect(rc3).to_equal(0)
expect(out3).to_contain("bootstrap-plan: execution=not-attempted")
expect(rt_file_exists(receipt)).to_equal(true)
val (out4, rc4) = run_planner("//bootstrap:stage4", "self-host-convergence-check", receipt,
    sha64("a"), sha64("b"), sha64("c"), sha64("d"))
expect(rc4).to_equal(0)
# Every other target prefix is denied, fail-closed.
val (outR, rcR) = run_planner("//release:stage4", "seed-missing", receipt,
    sha64("a"), sha64("b"), sha64("c"), sha64("d"))
expect(rcR).to_equal(2)
expect(outR).to_contain("bootstrap-policy-error: typed-reason-required")
val (outA, rcA) = run_planner("//bootstrap:stage2", "seed-missing", receipt,
    sha64("a"), sha64("b"), sha64("c"), sha64("d"))
expect(rcA).to_equal(2)
expect(outA).to_contain("bootstrap-policy-error: typed-reason-required")
```

</details>

#### requires all four binding hashes

- Verify: requires all four binding hashes
   - Expected: rcShort equals `2`
   - Expected: rcEmpty equals `2`
   - Expected: rt_file_exists(receipt) is false
   - Expected: rcOk equals `0`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 30 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-GEN-COMPILER-001
step("Verify: requires all four binding hashes")
val receipt = "build/land11_spec_fx/planner_badhash_receipt.txt"
if rt_file_exists(receipt):
    rt_file_delete(receipt)
# Admitted target+reason but a malformed parent hash must be denied.
val (outShort, rcShort) = run_planner("//bootstrap:stage3", "seed-missing", receipt,
    "deadbeef", sha64("b"), sha64("c"), sha64("d"))
expect(rcShort).to_equal(2)
expect(outShort).to_contain("bootstrap-policy-error: admission-hash-required")
# A missing planner hash (empty string) must also be denied.
val (outEmpty, rcEmpty) = run_planner("//bootstrap:stage3", "seed-missing", receipt,
    sha64("a"), sha64("b"), sha64("c"), "")
expect(rcEmpty).to_equal(2)
expect(outEmpty).to_contain("bootstrap-policy-error: admission-hash-required")
expect(rt_file_exists(receipt)).to_equal(false)
# With all four valid hashes the receipt carries the v2 marker and
# every binding hash.
val ok_receipt = "build/land11_spec_fx/planner_ok_receipt.txt"
if rt_file_exists(ok_receipt):
    rt_file_delete(ok_receipt)
val (_out, rcOk) = run_planner("//bootstrap:stage3", "seed-missing", ok_receipt,
    sha64("a"), sha64("b"), sha64("c"), sha64("d"))
expect(rcOk).to_equal(0)
val receipt_text = rt_file_read_text(ok_receipt) ?? ""
expect(receipt_text).to_contain("simple-bootstrap-authorization-v2")
expect(receipt_text).to_contain("parent_sha256=" + sha64("a"))
expect(receipt_text).to_contain("runtime_sha256=" + sha64("b"))
expect(receipt_text).to_contain("source_closure_sha256=" + sha64("c"))
expect(receipt_text).to_contain("planner_sha256=" + sha64("d"))
```

</details>

